version: "2.0"
description: >-
  Gnomon — the Paradigm 8.0 kernel (docs/specs/gnomon.md). One daemon per user
  owning sessions, identity, the hash-chained log, approvals, the budget fuse
  and the localhost web endpoint; bins gnomon, gnomond and gnomon-web. PR-0
  SCAFFOLD (research 29 §1/§4): the §18 layout with a src/ prefix, placeholder
  bins that print their version, the import fence, the zero-deps check, the
  G-WIN-05 registry skeleton and the M1.0 probe harness. Node >= 24 for Gnomon
  packages only; private and outside the root build/test scripts until the 8.0
  cut (G-MIG-01) — use `npm run build:gnomon` / `npm run test:gnomon`. Will ship
  later as a signed Node SEA (tsup emits one self-contained file per entry).

components:
  gnomon-kernel:
    description: >-
      The kernel package. ZERO runtime deps (G-SEC-01): package.json has no
      `dependencies` key; @a-company/gnomon-contracts is a devDependency that
      tsup bundles. Import fence (G-KRN-02): every import under src/kernel/**
      is node:*, relative, or @a-company/gnomon-contracts, and dist/ holds no
      bare import. src/kernel/ has the thirteen §18 modules (identity, log,
      runner, supervisor, broker, budget, scheduler, manifest, refs, socket,
      web, sandbox, modhost) as empty directories at PR-0. Placeholder bins
      write to stdio directly: the kernel cannot depend on the Paradigm logger
      (zero deps); #kernel-log brings its own logging at M1.2.
    path: src/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, kernel, paradigm-8, scaffold]
    components:
      - "#gnomon-probes"
    tests:
      - test/fence.test.ts
      - test/sec-01.test.ts
      - test/platform-registry.test.ts
      - test/version.test.ts
    oracles: [G-KRN-02, G-SEC-01, G-WIN-05]

  gnomon-probes:
    description: >-
      M1.0 probe harness (spec §19.1, research 29 §2). `node
      packages/gnomon/probes/run.mjs <id> [--out-dir d] [--timeout ms]` imports
      probes/<id>/probe.mjs (zero deps, no build), runs its default export with
      {id, platform, arch, probeDir, signal}, and writes a probeResult:v1 record
      to probes/results/<id>.<platform>.json. Throws and timeouts become verdict
      `fail`. Exit codes 0 pass / 1 fail / 2 partial / 64 usage. Probe ids match
      ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$ (no path traversal). p-harness is the self-test and
      its results are gitignored; real results are committed from hardware runs
      only. A `fail` on a ruling means a re-plan memo before dependent builds.
      Unsigned macOS probes: p10m-sbx-deny-mac (S29-03/04 sandbox-exec session
      denies + escape matrix), p11-ws-framing (RFC 6455 over node:http with a
      forked server child, 27 Autobahn-style raw cases, 4 MiB throughput, RSS
      and phys_footprint), p-noise-vectors (Noise IK/XX/XXpsk3 over node:crypto
      against a verbatim cacophony/snow vector subset in vectors.json, G-LNK-11)
      and p01-claude-cli (read-only `claude --version`/`--help` flag check;
      live items pending-manual).
    path: probes/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, probes, m1.0]
    tests:
      - test/probe-harness.test.ts
